---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const { name } = SITE;
const { legalName, email, address } = SITE.business;
---

<Policy title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${name} handles your data: invoices and emails are processed only in your browser.`}>
  <p>
    This policy explains what data {name} (the “extension”) and this website handle, operated by <strong>{legalName}</strong>
    (“we”, “us”). The short version: <strong>your emails and invoices are processed only inside your own browser. We never receive them.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>1. What the extension accesses</h2>
  <p>When you start a scan, the extension reads the Gmail pages open in your browser to find invoice, receipt and bill emails in the period you choose. It then:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>downloads the matching PDF attachments, or the email text for receipts with no attachment, <strong>into your browser’s memory</strong>;</li>
    <li>reads details such as date, vendor, amount, currency, tax ID (e.g. GSTIN) and invoice number from them, <strong>on your computer</strong>;</li>
    <li>saves a ZIP file of renamed PDFs and a summary spreadsheet to <strong>your Downloads folder</strong>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Email content, attachments and extracted details are <strong>not sent to us or to anyone else</strong>. They are discarded from memory when the scan or export ends.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What is stored on your device</h2>
  <p>The extension saves the following in your browser’s local extension storage, so it works the same next time:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your settings (file name format, folder layout, date format, currency, financial-year start);</li>
    <li>your sender choices (vendor names you set, senders you chose to skip);</li>
    <li>your license key and its activation status.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can delete all of this at any time by removing the extension.</p>

  <h2>3. What leaves your device</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>License check.</strong> Your license key and an anonymous activation ID are sent to our payment provider, Dodo Payments, to confirm the
      license is valid and to count activations (up to {SITE.devicesPerLicense} browsers per license).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Compatibility settings.</strong> The extension may download a small settings file from this website that tells it how to find
      items on the Gmail page. Like any web request, our hosting provider (Cloudflare) may log your IP address and browser type for security.
      No email data is included.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The extension contains no analytics, advertising or tracking code.</p>

  <h2>4. Google user data</h2>
  <p>
    Version 1 of the extension does not use Google APIs and does not ask you to sign in with Google. If a future version offers Google Drive export,
    it will ask for your permission first, request only access to files it creates, and our use of information received from Google APIs will adhere
    to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements. We will update this policy before that happens.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are handled by Dodo Payments, which acts as our merchant of record. Dodo Payments collects your name, email address, billing details
    and payment information under its own privacy policy. We receive your name, email address, country and order details so we can send your license
    key, provide support and handle refunds. We never see your full card details.
  </p>

  <h2>6. This website</h2>
  <p>
    This website is a static site hosted on Cloudflare Pages. It does not use cookies, analytics or third-party trackers. Fonts are served from this
    site, not from Google Fonts. Cloudflare may process your IP address to deliver and protect the site.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Emails from us</h2>
  <p>
    We use your email address to send your license key, beta access, important product updates and support replies. We don’t send marketing emails
    without your consent, and we don’t sell or share your email address.
  </p>

  <h2>8. How long we keep data</h2>
  <p>
    We keep order and license records for as long as your license is active and as required for tax and accounting law. Support emails are kept
    for up to 2 years. We hold no email or invoice content from your inbox, so there is nothing of that kind to keep or delete.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live (for example under India’s Digital Personal Data Protection Act, the EU/UK GDPR or California law), you may have the
    right to access, correct or delete the personal data we hold about you, or to object to how we use it. Email <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
    and we will respond within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>{name} is a business tool and is not intended for anyone under 18.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we will update the date at the top. If a change is significant, for example a new kind of data leaving your device, we will email customers before it applies.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {legalName}<br />
    {address}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
  </p>
</Policy>
